      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The numbers like 10-10-10 represent the percentage by weight of Nitrogen (N), Phosphorus ($\\text{P}_2\\text{O}_5$), and Potassium ($\\text{K}_2\\text{O}$) in the fertilizer. Nitrogen is crucial for green, leafy growth, while Phosphorus helps with root development and overall vigor. Yellowing leaves could indicate a nitrogen deficiency, but brown patches might signal a potassium issue or soil dryness. To be sure, check the soil drainage and moisture levels first before guessing the nutrient imbalance.",
